Open Policy Agent
-----------------

Open Policy Agent is published by the OPA Authors in
https://github.com/open-policy-agent/opa under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
This repository holds OPA's tree at the release v1.22.2 (commit
482d9e368c2ddfed67ced59259fa6a247bb5f1e5), unchanged.

src/opa/schema/ models eight of OPA's JSON formats. scripts/opa_to_linkml.py writes it
from OPA's files: the JSON Schemas v1/ir/plan.schema.json,
v1/bundle/manifest.schema.json and v1/schemas/authorizationPolicy.json; the
data files capabilities.json, capabilities/, builtin_metadata.json and
v1/ast/version_index.json; v1/ir/ir.go; and the Go structs and constants of
v1/plugins/logs/plugin.go, v1/plugins/status/plugin.go,
v1/plugins/bundle/status.go, v1/plugins/logs/status/status.go,
v1/plugins/plugins.go and v1/bundle/bundle.go. The structure of the schema is
this project's. The descriptions of the plan classes that match a type in
v1/ir/ir.go open with that type's doc comment. The description of the
authorization input's class and that of the plan's legacy Index key come from
OPA's JSON Schemas. Those doc comments and these two descriptions are OPA's
words. The other descriptions are this project's.
src/opa/datamodel/, project/ and docs/schema/ are generated from the schema.

tests/data/captured/ holds documents OPA's release image wrote when
scripts/capture_opa_documents.py ran it on this project's test policies.

